WEBVTT

00:21:27.004 --> 00:21:31.668
From that viewpoint, what does it mean
to try to make life better?

00:21:31.692 --> 00:21:33.382
DB: Well, there's no silver bullet.

00:21:33.406 --> 00:21:35.474
We're recording this
on 4th Street, I think.

00:21:35.498 --> 00:21:37.750
If you traveled half a mile west,

00:21:37.774 --> 00:21:41.266
you get to the neighborhood where
Jane Jacobs lived in the 1950s and '60s,

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:43.337
the West Village in New York City.

00:21:43.361 --> 00:21:47.135
She wrote this beautiful passage
about the street as a ballet,

00:21:47.159 --> 00:21:49.568
that in the morning
the garbage men come through,

00:21:49.592 --> 00:21:52.283
then the moms are coming out
taking out the trash,

00:21:52.307 --> 00:21:54.225
then, the fruit man comes.

00:21:54.249 --> 00:21:57.949
And so, there's always eyes on the street,
and it's this organic ballet.

00:21:57.973 --> 00:22:00.711
And that's the beauty of a community;
it's like a ballet.